      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T16:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed in PS2: `make-sob` makes the table from the equality predicate when the comparator can\u0027t hash. `(set (make-comparator #t string\u003d? #f #f) \"a\" \"b\" (string #\\a))` has size 2, and so do the eq?, eqv?, equal? and string-ci\u003d? cases. `set-comparator` hashes all five, and a lambda predicate is still refused.",
      "parentUuid": "eb360421_67b4e9cf",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
