      },
      "lineNbr": 1308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1040172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`sob-hash` hashes each element with the element comparator\u0027s hash. With the default comparator that is `default-hash`, which starts a fresh budget on every call. Since `set-comparator` is registered (1323), a set that reaches itself through a vector never finishes hashing:\n\n```scheme\n(define v (vector #f)) (define s (set c v)) (vector-set! v 0 s) (default-hash v)\n```\n\nThis was still running after 30 s, while a plain circular vector hashes at once. 128.sld promises that deep and circular data cannot hang its hashes. Hash the size plus a bounded number of element hashes.\n\nSeparately, `sob-fold` visits each element of a bag once per copy, so hashing a bag costs its total count, not its unique size. Add `count × hash(element)` once per entry, modulo the limit.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c244b9ac_b91c89db",
        "filename": "crates/vali-compiler/lib/srfi/113.sld",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1040172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T16:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Partly fixed. Hashing now ends, and a bag costs its unique size: a bag holding 16,000 copies of one element hashes in 0.01 s. But each of the three levels still hashes every element. So a set of n boxes that each hold the set costs n + n² + n³ element hashes. A bag costs more, because `sob-size` walks a bag\u0027s table even at the cut-off:\n\n```scheme\n(define bc (make-comparator vector? eq? #f\n             (lambda (b) (if (vector-ref b 0) (comparator-hash set-comparator (vector-ref b 0)) 0))))\n(define s (list-\u003eset bc boxes))   ; n boxes, each (vector #f i)\n(for-each (lambda (b) (vector-set! b 0 s)) boxes)\n(comparator-hash set-comparator s)\n```\n\n- Set, n \u003d 10 / 20 / 40: 1,110 / 8,420 / 65,640 element hashes, 0.05 / 0.23 / 1.82 s.\n- The same with `list-\u003ebag` and `bag-comparator`: 0.21 / 3.18 / 49.3 s.\n- Through `default-hash` with `set-comparator` registered, a set of n vectors holding it takes 0.11 / 0.83 / 4.82 s. The same with hashmaps (hash.sld:471) takes 0.11 / 0.90 / 6.69 s.\n\nThe regression test (srfi-113-sets-and-bags.scm:796) uses a one-element set, so this doesn\u0027t show there. Hash the elements of the outermost sob only, and count a nested one by `(%tab-size ...)`. That makes it linear and still agrees with `set\u003d?` and `bag\u003d?`. Do the same in the hashmap hash.",
      "parentUuid": "5eb4d85b_8352f289",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
