        "id": 1040172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Registering these changes `default-hash` for the whole program. (srfi 128) (128.sld:347) hashes with `%equal-hash` until something is registered and with `%slow-hash` after, and this is the first standard library to register (146 does too).\n\nSo a table built with the default comparator before (srfi 113) loads loses its keys:\n\n```scheme\n;; (mylib table): (define table (make-hash-table (make-default-comparator)))\n;;                (hash-table-set! table \u0027(1 2 3) \u0027value)\n(import (scheme base) (scheme write) (srfi 125) (mylib table) (srfi 113))\n(write (hash-table-ref/default table \u0027(1 2 3) \u0027missing))\n```\n\nThis prints `missing`, and `value` without the (srfi 113) import. Default hashing of structures also gets much slower once `%slow-hash` takes over.\n\nThe spec doesn\u0027t require registering: post-finalization note 3 removed it. Don\u0027t register, or first make `default-hash` give the same answer whether or not anything is registered (in 128). That would be a change of its own, ahead of this one.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
