        "id": 1040172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Suggestion: `mapping-catenate` trusts its precondition, and breaking it corrupts the mapping for good. `(mapping-catenate c (mapping c 5 \u0027a) 1 \u0027b (mapping c 0 \u0027z))` gives an alist of `((5 . a) (1 . b) (0 . z))`, after which `mapping-contains?` on 5 is #f and `mapping-set` on 5 makes a second 5. The spec only says \"it is an error\", but checking max(m1) \u003c key \u003c min(m2) costs O(log n) and turns the corruption into an error.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
