      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`%set!` keeps the old key when the new one is equal under the comparator. With a string-ci comparator, `(hashmap-keys (hashmap-set (hashmap ci \"A\" 1) \"a\" 2))` gives `(\"A\")`, where `mapping-set` gives `(\"a\")`. The spec says the previous association \"is deleted\", and `hashmap-replace` already deletes first for that reason (165). This affects `hashmap-set(!)`, `-update(!)` and `-update/default(!)`. Delete the key before `hash-table-set!`.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
